00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,000
In order to make it easier to arrange, first hide the window in the library.

2
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Click on the 2D arrangement tool to reset the 3D window to the 2D window.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Click on the display arrangement icon in the 3D window vertical view menu.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
You can see that the virtual model has appeared around the blue points that are used to arrange the panels.

5
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Press Ctrl A to select all panels. After clicking on the panel, the positioning ball that can control the position of the panel will appear.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Drag the green axis of the positioning ball to move all panels to the position of the arrangement point without blocking.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Drag the other axis on the positioning ball to move in other directions.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Click and drag the yellow square in the positioning ball to move in the plane.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Drag the circle on the positioning ball to move in the plane.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Click and drag the circle to move in the plane.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Press Ctrl C to cancel the procedure.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The default positioning ball is based on the perspective of the lens.

13
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:22,000
In the menu bar in the 3D background, you can change the positioning ball coordinates.

14
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The horizontal coordinates are based on the horizontal coordinates of the selected object.

15
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The horizontal coordinates are based on the horizontal coordinates of the selected object.

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:45,539
The horizontal coordinates are based on the

17
00:01:45,539 --> 00:01:47,000
The horizontal coordinates are fixed.

18
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:53,000
The horizontal coordinates are fixed.

19
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:03,000
When arranging a board, its symmetrical board will also be arranged in the same way.

20
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Since the board has a positive and a negative side, please check the board transparency when arranging the back of the board to prevent mistakes.

21
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:30,000
After arranging the board, you can adjust its properties in the property editor.

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Drag and drop the adjustment axis to rotate or move the board.

23
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,000
When a board property is modified, the other symmetrical board will also be modified.

24
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Adjusting the axis can make the board close or far from the model.

25
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:07,000
Changing the direction can make the board rotate in one direction.

26
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:12,000
You can also use the positioning tool to adjust the position of the board after arranging.

27
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:22,000
However, the position of the positioning tool will not be applied to the symmetrical board.

28
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Press the Shift key and click on the board, you can select more boards.

29
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:31,000
It is recommended that if you use the positioning tool to modify the 3D position, you can modify the position of two boards at the same time.

30
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:37,000
You can see that if you continue to display the arrangement points after arranging the board, it will be more inconvenient.

31
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Therefore, after arranging the board, please hide the arrangement points.

32
